Top Recommendation: NormCap
NormCap is the closest equivalent because it is "stateless"—it doesn't open a main window first; it just puts the screen into "capture mode" immediately upon launch. 

Install via Flatpak:
bash>>
  flatpak install flathub com.github.dynobo.normcap

Set the Shortcut: Open your system's Keyboard Settings -> Custom Shortcuts and create a new one:
Name: Text Extractor
Command: flatpak run com.github.dynobo.normcap
Shortcut: Super + Shift + T (Note: Super is your Windows key).

How it works: When you press the shortcut, a red border appears. Select your text, and it is automatically copied to your clipboard. 
